1.create user.
2.siva can send his public key to admin user.
3./home/siva admin creates .ssh in /home/siva folder.
4.siva is only owner to this folder 700.
5.create a file called authorized.keys with access 600.
6.admin keeps siva public key here.
7.now siva should be able to login with key.

steps
----
sudo su 
useradd siva
cd ../siva
mkdir .ssh
chmod 700 -R .ssh/
cd .ssh/
touch authorized_keys
create key (ssh-keygen -f siva)
vi authorized_keys
chmod 600 authorized_keys
cd ..
chown siva:siva -R .ssh
cd .ssh
cmd (To login)
ssh -i siva siva@<ip>
id siva

To give root access to user
---------------------------
vim /etc/sudoers (uncomment pwd)
usermod -aG wheel siva
id siva
exit

Again login
-----------
ssh -i siva siva@<ip>
sudo useradd suresh
